      "detail": "Supplied usage bytes match current repository public example. All four usage runs consume monthly_data_processed_gb=100, increasing NAT data quantity from 0 to 100 and static charge by 4.5. Bucket storage_gb=1 and repository storage_gb=10 leave quantities zero; served catalog requires monthly_storage_gb instead. This is initial Infracost-style usage-schema incompatibility, NOT evidence of an inherent GCS/Artifact Registry storage-pricing failure. Separate native-correct usage rechecks being performed by the parent are outside this completed run's acceptance evidence. Bucket operation inputs have no corresponding dimensions. NAT supplied assigned_vms differs from served active_vms; equal default 1 masks that mismatch. Compute monthly_hrs=730 equals default, so unchanged 730 quantity is not independent proof this key was consumed. NAT pricing is static in served definitions and output, not a catalog-backed live GCP NAT quote."
