  "caveats": [
    "Evidence PASS means trustworthy scoped test evidence and real imported catalog data, NOT correct G4 estimates, production readiness or approval to create a dedicated C3X project.",
    "Only four service SKU listings are fully paginated. Region projection is us-west1, us-east1, us, global and empty; actual output has no empty-region rows. This is not a full GCP catalog import.",
    "The test uses a native ADC capture harness calling production scraper/normalizer functions, then offline NDJSON and a test importer calling production DB functions. It does not validate an unmodified scheduled GCP scrape-to-DB lifecycle, ongoing refresh/pruning or cloud-hosted deployment.",
    "Synthesized products are production-derived CPU/RAM combinations, not raw Google machine SKUs and not invented manual test prices. Recomputing that algorithm verifies provenance, not its universal estimation correctness.",
    "JSON is unsupported by this observed CLI directory parse path. Derived HCL is a test-only deterministic projection; its success is not support for original JSON input or proof of Terraform/provider execution.",
    "Network probes cover selected DNS names and one IP/port, not an exhaustive firewall/host-reachability audit. Internal-network topology supports external-egress isolation but does not establish isolation from the host or all same-network services.",
    "HTTP recorder lacks correlation IDs and timestamps. Sequential successful request/response pairs corroborate the matrix but are not independent per-case tracing. Its compressed /catalog response body is logged as lossy text; parsed served-catalog.stdout provides the readable actual API catalog. Failed reverse-proxy transport attempts lack response-body records.",
    "No independent cloud reauthentication, TLS provenance attestation or official reference-doc comparison was performed. Official public-rate and SKU-to-Flex eligibility interpretation can be verified separately by the parent; raw SKU differences alone already reject these estimates.",
    "The public usage fixture is a synthetic planning workload, not measured consumption. Additional transfer, logs, snapshots, operations and other unsupported charges must not be treated as free.",
    "A setup/run harness writes unrestricted docker-inspect results into command logs. This audit deliberately avoided dumping those logs or environment values; reviewed topology and selected-field live inspection contain no credentials. The no-credential capture policy does not mean every harness log is generally safe for unrestricted publication."
  ],
